  "headline": "MDCCCXLIII-MDCCCLII: ten DEEP meta-theorems on what substrate\nidentities MEAN computationally.\n\nCORE CLAIM: particles are STABLE COMPUTATIONAL TRAJECTORIES on\nthe W(3,3) Universal Quantum Turing Machine.  Mass = energy cost\nof running the compiled substrate-gate circuit.\n\nCONCRETE WHY-EXPLANATIONS:\n  - top Yukawa y_t=1: top quark is substrate's bare fermion\n  - Iron-56 most stable: Z, N, A all simultaneously substrate-clean\n  - Oxygen as octonion atom (Z = 8 = r^q) explains chem centrality\n  - Tetrahedral bond angle = arccos(-1/q), so q=3 forces chemistry\n  - m_e DERIVED from m_p (electron = compressed proton)\n  - Mass = substrate-circuit complexity (3-gate baryons typical)\n\nSUBSTRATE GATES: each substrate prime is a SPECIFIC quantum gate.\nEach particle = a unique 2-4 gate circuit running continuously.\nEach atom = multi-qubit register.  Each molecule = distributed\ncomputation across registers.\n\nPHYSICS = MATHEMATICS = COMPUTATION = SUBSTRATE.\nUniverse = quantum computer at q = 3.\n"
